<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Vodni 1996 net drops to CZK 100 mln.</title>
<headline>Czech Vodni 1996 net drops to CZK 100 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>After-tax profit of the Czech construction conglomerate Vodni Stavby Praha a.s. in 1996 fell to 100 million crowns from 169.6 million the previous year, the company's financial director said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Zeno Veselik told Reuters that the company's board of directors would propose a 45 crown per share gross dividend on 1996 profit, the same as in 1995.</p>
